Z||000016||Songman||09-19-2000||09:40 AM||||Thanks MM. You will keep us informed if you hear any good news from Scott, won't you? Please, please, please...||||reg||14
Z||000017||stsmithgt||09-19-2000||12:02 PM||||I've tugged on my keys enough to turn off my dingy thingy, but I didn't know they could come completely out.  I'll have to try that.  I'd rather do that then wear out my starter over getting into the trunk or running back into the house for something I've forgotten. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000018||Standard||09-19-2000||10:24 PM||||My key's come out with the car running, too.  I always figured that the key was just worn down...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000019||Shadow Wolf||09-20-2000||01:43 AM||||If I want to get into the trunk while the engine is running, I generally use the power trunk release, now I know not everyone has one, but before you say, "It don't work with the engine running," it will if you put the parking brake on.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||Monkeyman||09-20-2000||09:29 PM||||If you have an automatic, just put it in park.||||reg||1
